# XSH tcsendbreak()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Terminal tests use a pseudo-terminal (XSI). The break duration is observable only on an
# asynchronous serial line, which a pseudo-terminal is not; whether the call does anything
# there is implementation-defined, so only its return value is checked.

assertion  XSH.tcsendbreak.001
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcsendbreak(fd, 0) on a pseudo-terminal subsidiary returns 0 (a
           pseudo-terminal is not asynchronous serial, so no timing is required;
           the call is bounded by an alarm).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/001-duration-zero.c

assertion  XSH.tcsendbreak.002
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcsendbreak(fd, 1) on a pseudo-terminal subsidiary returns 0 (the
           period is implementation-defined; the call is bounded by an alarm).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/002-duration-nonzero.c

assertion  XSH.tcsendbreak.003
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       tcsendbreak(-1) and tcsendbreak() of a closed descriptor return -1
           with EBADF.
test       t/003-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcsendbreak.004
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      1988
says       tcsendbreak() of descriptors for a regular file, both ends of a pipe
           and /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/004-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcsendbreak.005
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in a background process group (not orphaned) whose SIGTTOU
           is neither blocked nor ignored and which calls tcsendbreak() on its
           controlling terminal is sent SIGTTOU (default action: stopped).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/005-bg-sigttou.c

assertion  XSH.tcsendbreak.006
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in a background process group which calls tcsendbreak() on
           its controlling terminal while SIGTTOU is blocked, and again while it
           is ignored, completes normally (returns 0), is not stopped.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    60
test       t/006-bg-quiet.c

assertion  XSH.tcsendbreak.007
anchor     functions/tcsendbreak.html#ERRORS/EIO
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      2001
says       A process in an orphaned process group, with SIGTTOU neither blocked
           nor ignored, which calls tcsendbreak() on its controlling terminal
           gets -1 with EIO.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/007-orphan-eio.c
